{% block usage %}
The goal is a native Linux driver for the Tobii Eye Tracker 5 that gives
Star Citizen head tracking under Wine. **It has not yet run against a tracker
on Linux, and the game-side connection under Wine is unsolved.**

Everything here is rebuilt from Tobii's installed binaries and the tracker on
the Windows reference host `albedo`. No other ET5 driver project was used. Most
components are checked against the original machine code by emulating it on
synthetic inputs; those checks are listed in the linked documents.

## What exists

| Stage | Module | Status |
| --- | --- | --- |
| USB transport, channel framing | `usb.py`, `usb_framing.py`, `usb_channel.py` | Descriptor probe tested; channel index for TTP unverified |
| TTP requests and replies | `ttp.py`, `ttp_commands.py`, `ttp_fields.py` | Startup, unlock, realm, hardware info and stream commands match the original encoders and parsers |
| Camera calibration reply | `camera_info.py` | Parser matches the original; no device reply seen yet |
| Image frames | `frames.py` | Stream 0x501 layout recovered; frame route unverified |
| Face finder | `face_detect.py` | Matches the original detector end to end, network input included |
| Tracking loop and working view | `face_tracking.py` | Working view matches the original; LBF eye refinement not yet run |
| D1 landmarks, confidence gate | `d1.py`, `d1_quality.py` | Crop and gate match the original |
| Face-model fit | `pose_*.py` | Updates, bounds and staged caller match the original; temporal caller in progress |
| Output conversion, geometry, smoothing | `pose_output.py`, `pose_geometry.py`, `head_pose_pipeline.py` | Euler conversion, geometry stage and One Euro filters match the original |
| Device session and CLI | `driver.py`, `cli.py` | Tested only against a scripted fake device |
| Game client protocol (PRP) | `prp.py`, `prp_session.py` | Codecs and handshake match the game DLL; Wine delivery unsolved |

A public-domain portrait run through detection, landmarks and fitting gives a
frontal, stable pose, which is a sanity check, not a tracking result.

## Use

Probe for the tracker (no interface is claimed):

```sh
PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m tobii_linux.cli probe
```

Experimental head-pose session. It needs NumPy and OpenVINO, the models in
`models/tobii-et5`, and the display area in millimetres in Stream Engine's
corner order (top-left, top-right, bottom-left):

```sh
PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m tobii_linux.cli headpose \
  --display -296.62 326 111.82 300.38 326 111.82 -296.62 10.27 -3.1
```

It prints one JSON line per camera frame. The session sends commands to the
device; it has not been tried on real hardware.

## Tests

```sh
PYTHONPATH=.local/inference:src python3 -m unittest discover -s tests
PYTHONPATH=.local/python:.local/inference:src python3 tools/<oracle>.py
```

The oracles need the private Windows binaries under `evidence/private/` and
the Unicorn emulator; unit tests skip what they cannot run.

## NixOS

```sh
nix build path:.#default
```

Import `inputs.tobii-linux.nixosModules.default` and set
`hardware.tobii-eye-tracker-5.enable = true;` to install the command and a udev
rule granting the active seat user access to `2104:0313`. The flake has not
been evaluated yet; no NixOS machine is available.

